  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Uruguayans have two surnames on paper, father's then mother's (Martina Rodríguez Techera), but in daily life most go by the first one. Two given names are common (Juan Pablo, María Noel). Families are mostly of Spanish, Canary Island and Galician origin (Píriz, Techera, De León, Olivera are very Uruguayan) or Italian, with many Ligurian surnames in Montevideo (Ferrando, Peirano, Canessa, Raffo). Near the Brazilian border Portuguese surnames like Pereira, Da Silva and Machado are everywhere.",
